<title>FRANCE: Seita stock up after U.S. RJR verdict.</title>
<headline>Seita stock up after U.S. RJR verdict.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French tobacco company Seita rose on Tuesday after a Florida jury found that RJ Reynolds Tobacco was not negligent in a closely-watched wrongful death lawsuit.</p>
<p>Seita shares were up 2.33 percent at 206.70 francs at 1105 GMT, bolstered by rising stocks in U.S. tobacco companies.</p>
<p>The CAC-40 index was down 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
